On the winding road that climbs from Case Noyale up to Chamarel a lookout opens onto one of the finest views in Mauritius. You see the wide lagoon of the southwest with Île aux Bénitiers floating in it and the mass of Le Morne Brabant beyond.

It is an easy stop on the way to the Seven Coloured Earths and Chamarel Falls. Small stalls sometimes set up here.

## Good to know

- The road is narrow and busy with tourist traffic: park only in the parking area.
- The view is best in clear morning light before clouds build over the hills.
